{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You shall not curse the deaf.</b> Rashi explained: the same applies to any person, and Scripture specifies the deaf to tell you — just as the deaf is singled out in that he is alive, etc. And one may give a reason why Scripture specified the deaf in particular: because the Sages said (Bava Kamma 85b) — one who blinded his fellow's eye gives him the value of his eye; one who deafened him gives him the value of his all. And according to this premise there is room for error, to say that a deaf person is considered like a dead person and one is not liable for cursing him; from this inference you would learn that one is exempt for cursing the dead, and the deaf person is treated as alive with regard to the one who curses him. And one should not say that perhaps the intent of the verse is to obligate one who curses the dead, modeled on the deaf person who is considered like the dead — for if so, the verse should have remained silent and not said 'You shall not curse the deaf,' and I would hear from 'בְּעַמְּךָ לֹא תָאֹר' (Exodus 22:27) that everyone is included, whether alive or dead, for whence would you derive a distinction? Rather, it is certain that by Torah law one who curses the dead is exempt, and it might enter your mind that the deaf person too is included among the dead — for his deafness gives him the value of his all, for it is as though his entire existence were reduced to nothing and naught — therefore Scripture says 'You shall not curse the deaf,' and all like him who are alive, even though they are considered as dead, such as those four who are considered as dead that the Sages enumerated (Nedarim 64b) — for all of them he is liable." "<b>And before the blind you shall not place a stumbling block.</b> Rashi explained: do not give counsel, etc., for one cannot interpret 'blind' literally and 'stumbling block' literally, since it is written 'וְיָרֵאתָ מֵּאֱלֹהֶיךָ,' and this speaks of a matter that is surrendered to the heart specifically."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:37:32.333349826Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}